---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FactorLab from "../../components/FactorLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Factor Models (Fama–French)"
  description="Beyond CAPM: the Fama–French factors. Attribute a portfolio's expected return to size, value, profitability, and investment tilts, and watch CAPM's alpha become explained factor exposure."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Beyond beta: the factor zoo</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      CAPM says one thing drives returns: the market. But decades of data show
      small stocks, cheap "value" stocks, and profitable, conservative firms have
      all earned <em>more</em> than their market beta can explain. Fama and French
      turned those patterns into extra <strong>factors</strong> — and what CAPM
      called mysterious "alpha" became exposure you can dial on purpose.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <FactorLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The five factors</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Market (Mkt−RF)</strong> — the whole market's return over T-bills. CAPM's only factor.</li>
        <li><strong>Size (SMB)</strong> — small companies minus big.</li>
        <li><strong>Value (HML)</strong> — cheap stocks minus expensive ones.</li>
        <li><strong>Profitability (RMW)</strong> — robustly profitable firms minus weak.</li>
        <li><strong>Investment (CMA)</strong> — conservative firms minus aggressive.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A portfolio's <strong>loading</strong> (β) on each factor says how exposed
        it is. Multiply each loading by that factor's historical premium and you
        get its contribution to expected return. Switch from CAPM to the 3- and
        5-factor models and watch a tilted portfolio's "alpha" collapse into
        explained factor bets.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it gets hazy</h2>
      <p>
        Factor premia are real but <em>noisy and slippery</em>. Value spent much of
        the 2010s underwater; premia shrink after they're published; and with
        enough data-mining you can "discover" factors that are just luck. Treat
        these as tendencies over decades, not guarantees — and remember the
        <a href="/tools/superstocks">superstock problem</a>: even a good tilt still
        needs broad diversification.
      </p>
      <p>
        Premia and volatilities are long-run annualized US figures (≈1963–present)
        from the <a href="https://mba.tuck.dartmouth.edu/pages/faculty/ken.french/data_library.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kenneth French Data Library</a>;
        loadings are illustrative. Educational only, not advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextTool current="/tools/factors" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .fl-model {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 4px;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 4px;
  }
  .fl-model button {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .fl-model button.active {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .fl-group {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: var(--space-xs) 0 0;
  }
  .fl-dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .fl-dim {
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .fl-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .fl-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .fl-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .fl-headline-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .fl-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .fl-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .fl-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .fl-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
